Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/hdmi: add an opt-in single-pipe FRL path

Port patches 01–50 from [PATCH v2 00/56] Enable HDMI FRL for MTL+,
by Ankit Nautiyal, Suraj Kandpal and Vandita Kulkarni. Omit the HDMI
joiner and leave DSC unused for the first hardware qualification.

Keep native progressive RGB deep-color FRL opt-in and require explicit
firmware and sink capabilities. Preserve the old TMDS and CB1 metadata
paths. Use the selected protocol for PLL tables and SCDC ownership,
the negotiated cap after a failed training attempt, and reference-counted
retry work. Advertise only audio formats modeled by the FRL DFM.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/dri-devel/20261012035806.3361439-1-ankit.k.nautiyal@intel.com/

